{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts","id":9211,"title":"A couple of questions about pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T15:00:03-08:00","id":9211,"title":"A couple of questions about pacts","content":"So I've been thinking about pacts recently and I have a few questions.<br /> <br /> Lets say that Asmodeus buys Bob's relationshop with his wife Mary. What exactly does this feel like from Mary's perspective, how does she interpret suddenly being married to a different person?<br /> <br /> Now lets say that Asmodeus buys Alice's relationship with her completely homosexual wife Mary. How does Mary interpret suddenly being married to a Demon in a male Cover? What stops her from asking for a divorce about a day later?<br /> <br /> Finally, what if Mary was a powerful Magistos. Would her Mind magic protect her?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:12:30-08:00","id":9219,"title":"","content":"I'm nothing resembling a dev but I look at it a lot like Psychic Reprogramming (Assuming from the Mastigos reference I'm dealing with one familiar with high end Mind). This is just how it's always been, supernatural power says so. Regarding the homosexual female being married to a &quot;male&quot; all of a sudden, I imagine it's much the same just that there's a certain level of dissonance that comes up.<br /> <br /> The dissonance doesn't really strike me as a mechanics issue, but it does strike me as the source of a great many derangements.<br /> <br /> As far as the Mind Magic is concerned, I would rule that as long as the mind magic effect lasted (max a month) she would be protected. Once it lapses, protection lapses, and suddenly this problematic marriage seems a-ok.<br /> <br /> Just my $0.02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":323,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","user":"Hyoseph","date":". 11-12-2013, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:01:09-08:00","id":9259,"title":"","content":"To the first Mary, things are as they've always been. She rationalizes the changes made fairly easily, making any adjustments to her memories necessary to accommodate a different husband. She'll attribute memories of Bob to Asmodeus, even where that wouldn't entirely make sense if she described them to a third party.<br /> <br /> To the second Mary, things are much the same, except that she'll have a lot more trouble adjusting. She'll remember marrying a man, even if that now seems like an insane mistake. She'll attribute memories of Alice to Asmodeus, even if she now can't understand what she could possibly have been thinking.<br /> <br /> The first Mary could easily have serious dissonance being married to Asmodeus as well. Both of them will try to explain it to themselves... but the second Mary has a much more obvious problem to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:28:30-08:00","id":9376,"title":"","content":"Splicing yourself into Covers that you're going to have a hard time maintaining, BTW, is going to get said Covers eroded, especially if they push people to investigate you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T22:50:27-08:00","id":9491,"title":"","content":"not a question regarding pacts but... in the book its stated that the GM no when an angel falls it can quickly dispatch angels to capture the would be demon and reintegrate him, that doesn't bother me. Its also stated that the GM creates the covers for its angels, if that's the case wouldn't the GM just send angels after the demons cover assuming he escaped the first time? Or is it that the act of falling for an angel deletes knowledge of the demons cover from the GM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T23:53:20-08:00","id":9502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9491#post9491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not a question regarding pacts but... in the book its stated that the GM no when an angel falls it can quickly dispatch angels to capture the would be demon and reintegrate him, that doesn't bother me. Its also stated that the GM creates the covers for its angels, if that's the case wouldn't the GM just send angels after the demons cover assuming he escaped the first time? Or is it that the act of falling for an angel deletes knowledge of the demons cover from the GM?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book describes demons as somewhat altering and tweaking the Cover they previously had when they Fall. I imagine that altering and tweaking probably makes a lot of difference. Also, the system that sends out the hunter angels isn't necessarily the same one that crafted the Cover. Not all parts of the God Machine seem to talk to each other all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T02:21:31-08:00","id":9537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9491#post9491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not a question regarding pacts but... in the book its stated that the GM no when an angel falls it can quickly dispatch angels to capture the would be demon and reintegrate him, that doesn't bother me. Its also stated that the GM creates the covers for its angels, if that's the case wouldn't the GM just send angels after the demons cover assuming he escaped the first time? Or is it that the act of falling for an angel deletes knowledge of the demons cover from the GM?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact of falling removes the knowledge of the demons cover from the god machine. IF we use computers as a reference then the GMC is the computer who has a list of all files being part of its software (a list of filenames aka covers over which it knows all the details). The fall of a demon renames the file on the hard drive but not in the list, thus the GMC sees i its list a filename that poitns to a non existing file and knows someone has fallen but it doesn't find out who as it doesn't know the new name (so its missing a few search functions modern PCs now have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T04:14:17-08:00","id":9579,"title":"","content":"The other thing, is, it's not the GM has an unlimited supply of hunter angels just hanging around. Sending out hunter angels requires a lot of energy, and the GM has long since realized that having a demon on Earth <i>can</i> be useful. Better not to make a big mess just because an angel Fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T05:42:25-08:00","id":9604,"title":"","content":"Going back to Pacts: would it be a valid strategy to offer a Pact with a mortal that is heavily weighted toward benefitting the mortal (possibly even to the point of not including any benefit for the demon at all), and then to threaten to destroy the pact if the mortal doesn\u2019t do exactly what the demon demands of him? It would augment the mortal\u2019s potential usefulness immensely for a really low cost (one point of Willpower on the demon\u2019s part), and the amount of leverage it would give the demon would be directly proportional to how lopsided the deal is in the mortal\u2019s favor: for instance, a demon who agrees to grant the mortal permanent control over a multinational corporation in exachange for, say, taking ownership of the mortal\u2019s pet dog for a day would be in a tremendous position to blackmail the chief of a multinational corporation: sure, I\u2019ll lose your dog when I burn this contract (and not even that, if my day with your pet has already ended); but <i>you\u2019ll</i> lose all of that influence and power that I granted you if you don\u2019t do the following\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:09:55-08:00","id":9617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9604#post9604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to Pacts: would it be a valid strategy to offer a Pact with a mortal that is heavily weighted toward benefitting the mortal (possibly even to the point of not including any benefit for the demon at all), and then to threaten to destroy the pact if the mortal doesn\u2019t do exactly what the demon demands of him? It would augment the mortal\u2019s potential usefulness immensely for a really low cost (one point of Willpower on the demon\u2019s part), and the amount of leverage it would give the demon would be directly proportional to how lopsided the deal is in the mortal\u2019s favor: for instance, a demon who agrees to grant the mortal permanent control over a multinational corporation in exachange for, say, taking ownership of the mortal\u2019s pet dog for a day would be in a tremendous position to blackmail the chief of a multinational corporation: sure, I\u2019ll lose your dog when I burn this contract (and not even that, if my day with your pet has already ended); but <i>you\u2019ll</i> lose all of that influence and power that I granted you if you don\u2019t do the following\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like you just got Allies or a Retainer (or a Mentor, even?) out of the deal. So arguably, that should be included on your side of the bargain, cost-wise.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could argue that blackmail involving a Pact is not different to blackmail involving some other supernatural power. In which case I suppose it comes down to whether you allow players to get free merits because they &quot;earned&quot; them IC. (I would declare that they help you for this Chapter, and after that you have to pay XP or it falls apart.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:18:05-08:00","id":9660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9617#post9617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like you just got Allies or a Retainer (or a Mentor, even?) out of the deal. So arguably, that should be included on your side of the bargain, cost-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026except that the whole point of the blackmail is that these benefits <i>aren\u2019t</i> part of the contract. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9617#post9617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, you could argue that blackmail involving a Pact is not different to blackmail involving some other supernatural power. In which case I suppose it comes down to whether you allow players to get free merits because they &quot;earned&quot; them IC. (I would declare that they help you for this Chapter, and after that you have to pay XP or it falls apart.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh; that reminds me of Hero System\u2019s approach, putting the players\u2019 attention on managing the traits on their character sheet rather than roleplaying in a story. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T07:23:50-08:00","id":9668,"title":"","content":"And it goes against the GMC rules anyway. If you get hold of a merit without paying exp it's yours, you just don't get the sanctity of merits rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:31:32-08:00","id":9718,"title":"","content":"Even the \u201csanctity of merits\u201d section is more metagaming than I want to deal with; but yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:46:01-08:00","id":9730,"title":"","content":"I'm generally a fan of allowing merits to be earned for free <b>as well as</b> being paid for with xp. If anything Sanctity of Merits gives motivation to get things like social merits and retainers with xp. It's long been a perception that there's no point in buying the Retainer merit when they can just be kidnapped / killed by a (N)PC and thus cost xp that would have been &quot;better spent&quot; on superpowers. This leads to an &quot;Only spend xp on what you can't lose without dying&quot; mentality which imho is destructive to the game it comes up in.<br /> <br /> This way &quot;fixer&quot; and socialite characters can be made and played, their &quot;connections&quot; can be used for plot drama and character motivation, and they can't &quot;have their xp attacked&quot; by murdering their driver.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, a question - What happens to the signatories of a Major Pact / Cover during the time their identities are being worn by an Unchained and, equally importantly, afterwards? <br /> <br /> Using the Asmodeus example of Bob in the first post, what happens if Asmodeus/Bob goes on a 3 state killing spree (sabotaging the God Machine and its minions in the process, but the media doesn't know that) and then when the Hunters get too close, Asmodeus jumps out and on to the next person. What happens to Bob at that point? Is he back in a body and horrifically screwed? Has Bob been riding around in his own body forced to watch Asmodeus cutting a bloody swath through Wonderland? Or does the body just fall over because Bob was gone a long time ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T08:50:49-08:00","id":9734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyoseph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9730#post9730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on topic, a question - What happens to the signatories of a Major Pact / Cover during the time their identities are being worn by an Unchained and, equally importantly, afterwards?<br /> <br /> Using the Asmodeus example of Bob in the first post, what happens if Asmodeus/Bob goes on a 3 state killing spree (sabotaging the God Machine and its minions in the process, but the media doesn't know that) and then when the Hunters get too close, Asmodeus jumps out and on to the next person. What happens to Bob at that point? Is he back in a body and horrifically screwed? Has Bob been riding around in his own body forced to watch Asmodeus cutting a bloody swath through Wonderland? Or does the body just fall over because Bob was gone a long time ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean a Greater Cover +3 pact, or a Soul +3 pact? Greater Cover doesn't bodyjack, it just hands you over a precious piece of the person's history and life. Claiming a soul pact annihilates the person and integrates them as Cover \u2014 you can swap between Covers as normal, so the body doesn't &quot;fall over,&quot; it reconfigures into the new Cover and can be recovered later (heh). But Bob is gone, man. By claiming that pact, you killed him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:01:41-08:00","id":9744,"title":"","content":"Thanks SL - I've been working my way through the book as time allows and had a sneaking suspicion that was the case. Bob will be missed.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, he won't. He already sold off the people who would have missed him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/323-hyoseph","name":"Hyoseph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:55:54-08:00","id":9835,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Thus far, the Unchained don\u2019t do the Possession thing \u2014 though I could possibly see someone coming up with an Exploit along those lines. But Covers? That\u2019s not possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:24:37-08:00","id":9862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9835#post9835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Thus far, the Unchained don\u2019t do the Possession thing \u2014 though <b>I could possibly see someone coming up with an Exploit along those lines.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/possessionexploit.png\" target=\"_blank\">\u2026</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:10:01-08:00","id":10015,"title":"","content":"I actually have a question. Let's say I make little Pacts with somebody to benefit their life, stuff like additional wealth merits, social status, beauty, etc.<br /> <br /> Then I make a soul pact with him, and collect on it. Do I gain access to those benefits I gave him when he becomes a new Cover for me?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:35:52-08:00","id":10042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=9835#post9835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Thus far, the Unchained don\u2019t do the Possession thing \u2014 though I could possibly see someone coming up with an Exploit along those lines. But Covers? That\u2019s not possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is in fact an Exploit that does Possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:56:52-08:00","id":10050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=10042#post10042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is in fact an Exploit that does Possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two, possibly, if we count Ephemeral Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:07:57-08:00","id":10207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=10015#post10015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually have a question. Let's say I make little Pacts with somebody to benefit their life, stuff like additional wealth merits, social status, beauty, etc.<br /> <br /> Then I make a soul pact with him, and collect on it. Do I gain access to those benefits I gave him when he becomes a new Cover for me?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. When you take his soul, he ceases to exist; and destroying one of the participants in a pact is as sure a way to break the pact as destroying the contract itself. Heck, I\u2019d probably rule that <i>ordinary death</i> is enough to break a pact: even if your soul survives as a ghost, it\u2019s changed enough by the event that it\u2019s not the same person as far as demonic contracts are concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:12:40-08:00","id":10210,"title":"","content":"Here's a question I haven't gotten around to finding yet.<br /> <br /> When you collect on a soul pact, that person basically kapoots out. But that pact has to be on something written, and if it gets broken, then the contract is cancelled.<br /> <br /> 1)So if a soul pact's form is broken, does the person come back?<br /> 2)Can said contract be written on the person, and if so, what happens to it when collection calls come in?<br /> <br /> On the plus side, imagine making all your pacts a tattoo on the person you're dealing with. Having fun with that? You're welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T22:33:14-08:00","id":10217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=10210#post10210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)So if a soul pact's form is broken, does the person come back?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's left as a &quot;maybe.&quot; No Demon's managed to find out yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T23:18:10-08:00","id":10233,"title":"","content":"As with my previous post: once you\u2019ve taken a human\u2019s soul, there is no human on the other end of the contract; so there shouldn\u2019t be a contract to break anymore: the deal has been completed, and all that\u2019s left are its consequences (that is, your new Cover). That\u2019s my take, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T23:51:09-08:00","id":10246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=10233#post10233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with my previous post: once you\u2019ve taken a human\u2019s soul, there is no human on the other end of the contract; so there shouldn\u2019t be a contract to break anymore: the deal has been completed, and all that\u2019s left are its consequences (that is, your new Cover). That\u2019s my take, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the case for soul pacts, though. They explicitly still exist after being called in.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Like other pacts, this one alters reality, substituting the demon for the part agreed upon in the bargain. In the case of soul pacts, however, it is not just a part, but the entirety of a person\u2019s existence. They are annihilated from the universe mind, body and soul, gone beyond recall of any of a demon\u2019s magics. Perhaps there are some forces in the universe that can recall a person destroyed this way, but such vast cosmic powers are beyond the scope of a demon character.<b> Destroying the actual contract which binds the soul may return the destroyed person to existence, but if this is true, no demon has ever verified it. Such pacts are the most closely guarded of a demon\u2019s contracts. </b>The promise of a way back for a loved one or even a hated enemy (upon whom vengeance is no longer an option) might make an interesting basis for a chronicle, however, even if the rumor comes on the lips of a demon.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T00:49:50-08:00","id":10253,"title":"","content":"The book explains that demonic pacts are usually lopsided in the demon's favor. This makes sense, except for the fact that offering more doesn't actually cost the demon anything. Unless I misread it, it costs less willpower to give the mortal a fair deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:51:57-08:00","id":10307,"title":"","content":"That's a bit... weird. I would think least one demon would have tried it to experiment. If you already have a couple of covers, the payment other demons offer you might be worth more than a Cover. As for rumours, it's such an obvious thing to at least think about that most demons would have heard of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:01:36-08:00","id":10309,"title":"","content":"I'm not very fond of &quot;no one has ever tried this, so who knows what will happen&quot; rules, because it's really easy for a PC to go &quot;okay, fine. I try it. What happens?&quot; It really just pushes the responsibility of coming up with a good answer from the setting designer to the Storyteller. Which can be fine in some situations. Even if there's a good reason why something like that is undocumented, a hint as to <i>why</i> it's undocumented would be helpful. Suggestions of what <i>might</i> happen would be even better, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T06:46:27-08:00","id":10366,"title":"","content":"What might happen:<br /> <br /> 1) Nothing. Once the person is annihilated, they're out. Trying to pull them back is beyond anything's capability. It's like putting ashes back into paper form; you just can't. <br /> 2) The contract is broken, the Cover vanishes (which might Burn the demon), and the person returns to life, probably unaware anything happened.<br /> 3) As above, but the person's soul is gone, so the body comes back with <i>something else</i> in there (I love Intruders). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T07:38:06-08:00","id":10397,"title":"","content":"AKA, there is no real answer, it is up to ST fiat. I like that. It reminds me of the little sidebar about demonic children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:03:26-08:00","id":10410,"title":"","content":"To expand a little, it falls into the category of &quot;shit that would make for a really amazing chronicle or story, so don't let us step on your toes!&quot; There are things that I think absolutely do need to be nailed down so that the setting works, and then there's stuff that I think benefits from a little guided ambiguity. This is the latter, just IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:41:30-08:00","id":10438,"title":"","content":"To elaborate a little; I don't have any objection to guided ambiguity about burning soul pacts. It's when you try to put an IC reason for that ambiguity (demons never tried) that my brain goes &quot;hang on. That Doesn't make sense).<br /> <br /> If you instead outright said that the authors are leaving this one up to us readers, that would work without twinging by disbelief. It would also have the advantages that players don't go &quot;lets test it!&quot;, rather than being canonically unknown to demons it could be something the Unchained know the answer too. Just that the Storyteller chooses what that answer is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:45:14-08:00","id":10441,"title":"","content":"I think it's less presented as &quot;No one's EVER tried it&quot; and more as &quot;Sure maybe someone tried it but they're not exactly filing a report on it to you, plus Soul pacts are not exactly something you want to dick around with and poke with a stick just out of curiosity*&quot;<br /> <br /> *Hence the powerful and debilitating burst of pain if you lose one. And the fact that you ERASED SOMEONE to have this SHIELD AGAINST THE GOD-MACHINE'S WATCHING EYES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 11-14-2013, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:18:41-08:00","id":10485,"title":"","content":"Best answer there could be. I think the nature of which a person comes back in will be tied to where the cover is at-if it's low ,the person might not come back, keep it too high though and they might come back with some extra things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T13:34:32-08:00","id":10728,"title":"","content":"&quot;What if a demon tried it?&quot; is answerable with &quot;How would you be able to believe him when demons lie all the time and the only evidence specifically had to be destroyed to test it?&quot; I should think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T06:32:19-08:00","id":11221,"title":"","content":"Another pact question or more multiple ones:<br /> Lets say john has a wife that I want for my cover named Mark.<br /> I make a pact with john that gives mark the wife.<br /> <br /> Situation a.) John dies (murdered). Does the pact that gave me the wife get voided by this? (if so then long duration pacts with elderly ppl should never be made)<br /> <br /> Situation b.) John later on gets a soulpact with me that I use. Does the pact for the wife get voided by this?<br /> <br /> Situation c.) (If b says pact is not voided). I burn the cover for mike. What about the wife does she go back to john (thus pact for the wife cancelled?)?<br /> <br /> Situation d.) (also if b says pact is not voided). I burn the cover for john. What happens to the pact for his wife ? Does she try to go backc to her now non existing husband? Or what happens there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T16:38:36-08:00","id":11670,"title":"","content":"The exploit for Raise Dead p 259 indicates that demons use it in pacts with humans. Page 291 indicates that all benefits a demon can grant a mortal come from reality hacking that is automatically successful with the proper expenditures of willpower. <br /> <br /> Can demons resurrect family members through a pact without the Raise Dead exploit?<br /> <br /> Here's how I understand the rules so far: Giving a mortal a merit, healing damage, or removing persistent conditions (such as an illness), or increasing skills or attributes can be handled through the reality editing of the pact. Anything outside of that might require an embed or exploit. <br /> <br /> I would guess that a demon cannot grant immortality through any means that would add a major template to the mortal (Vampirism, etc), but the demon could do so by granting a merit based minor template, like as &quot;Thaumaturge&quot; or &quot;Psychic&quot;. Example: April asks the demon for immortality. The demon grants him the External Alchemy merit and tells David to start brewing immortality potions. <br /> <br /> Can pacts exist that don't involve reality hacking? Example: David Talbot doesn't just want to be immortal. He wants to be a Vampire, but since Louis won't turn him, he goes to Asmodeus for help. Asmodeus can't mystically transform David into a vampire since the mystery of Vitae isn't in the demon's purview, but he's had amicable dealings with Lestat, so he calls in a favor and has David embraced. <br /> <br /> Last question: Can a demon give a mortal the ability to use an embed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:23:09-08:00","id":11715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=11670#post11670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip* Last question: Can a demon give a mortal the ability to use an embed?</div> </div> </div> </div>After a fashion (and with some limitations), yes. They're called gadgets. They only get sketched out a little bit in the Core but from what I understand will get a more thorough treatment in a forthcoming book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T00:13:25-08:00","id":11936,"title":"","content":"While we're asking questions: So Sariel is making deals with college kids to build up their academic scores (and dots) and making sure they get bright shiny futures in exchange for a girlfriend here a bad breakup there, a limp (can you take a limp?) a wild night of debauchery there in the hopes of crafting a brand new cover, spending cover experience to build up from 0 to 5. (I'm assuming this is possible) my question is this: How does he get the covers name or face? you can't exactly buy them without a soul pact can you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T00:28:21-08:00","id":11940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=11936#post11936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're asking questions: So Sariel is making deals with college kids to build up their academic scores (and dots) and making sure they get bright shiny futures in exchange for a girlfriend here a bad breakup there, a limp (can you take a limp?) a wild night of debauchery there in the hopes of crafting a brand new cover, spending cover experience to build up from 0 to 5. (I'm assuming this is possible) my question is this: How does he get the covers name or face? you can't exactly buy them without a soul pact can you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wondering that myself. You can buy pieces of an identity and patch them together, but were do you get the physical body? Does one just kind of appear based off the parts you grafted together?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T01:44:02-08:00","id":11962,"title":"","content":"Demons can be creative, and probably have &quot;types&quot; they prefer. Besides, I can't imagine that a demon who's worked a patchwork cover all the way up to 5 dots is going to just outright ignore a piece of the cover he may well have to invent for herself. And let's face it, making up who you are is half the fun (for certain definitions of fun).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T08:28:35-08:00","id":12082,"title":"","content":"I feel Primum probably helps fill in little details like that in patchwork Covers.<br /> <br /> It DOES seem weird that a demon would normally tilt pact to favor himself more, given that it costs him nothing to improve the benefits for the mortal and in fact costs more Willpower to take the larger share of the benefits. Seems kinda stupid even. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:46:40-08:00","id":12180,"title":"","content":"I would like to see expanded Pact guidelines, but I think it makes sense that the game motivates you to give the mortal as fair a deal as possible since pacts work on a system of cosmic balance. You grant a mortal money, and someone else files bankruptcy. Trying to royally screw a human to benefit yourself on a deal can be done, but it takes effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T14:04:53-08:00","id":12281,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with the game encouraging a fair deal, but the statement that demons try to make a deal unfair when they get no benefit from such just seems kind of strangely out of character and dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T14:57:51-08:00","id":12312,"title":"","content":"If you make the deal have a time limit on their end then you can entice them to make further pacts to renew their benefits and get more benefits for yourself in the process. Not necessary with a soul pact because, well, you have everything you want from them, but with others...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T19:21:57-08:00","id":12434,"title":"","content":"You can't lie about the terms of the pacts, but I'm sure you can lie about your capability to form them. So offering small potatoes pacts while holding out better rewards as a benefit exclusive to a Soul Pact to make such a deal seem more tempting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T21:01:11-08:00","id":12478,"title":"","content":"I'm not terribly clear on when a pact stops being a going concern. Do I just keep accruing occult legal documents infinitely? Because there is going to get to a point where that's going to get difficult to track as player/Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T17:20:16-08:00","id":13702,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think there are any official rules for that. The way I intend to play it is to allow the participants to spend Experience to cement Benefits into their lives, effectively buying them after the fact. If the Pact is broken, whatever Benefits have been paid for with Experience remain; if all Benefits of a Pact have been paid for with Experience, then the Contract becomes moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T19:34:32-08:00","id":13743,"title":"","content":"I suppose the issue is permanent pacts. If you task yourself with providing someone a short term pact, such as say, a day of ridiculous wealth, at the end of that day you have completed the pact and it's not really a going concern. I'm just not sure how something like being erased from existence really gets undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T19:35:38-08:00","id":13744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9211-a-couple-of-questions-about-pacts?p=11940#post11940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been wondering that myself. You can buy pieces of an identity and patch them together, but were do you get the physical body? Does one just kind of appear based off the parts you grafted together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the physical appearance of a patch job accretes from elements of people you've taken pieces from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T04:37:19-08:00","id":14649,"title":"","content":"Heck, you could take the chemistry teacher's cancer plus give him status 3 (Drug Lord), for his soul. I bet he'd buy it.<br /> <br /> This is why Demons almost always go after the let's say... utterly miserable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}